# AUTHOR-PAREN PRESERVATION — the RUNNABLE ownership-sigil cells.
#
#   * `apply_once((^(int x): x + n), 3)` ... POS PIN, same mechanism on a move
#     CLOSURE argument. Re-emitted without the paren this is
#     `apply_once(^(int x): x + n, 3)`, which is REJECTED
#     (E_OwnershipMismatch) — the move-closure would become a moved argument.
#   * `ConsumeCallable[int(int)] g = (^(int x): x + 1)` ... RED on the pre-fix
#     binary, which deletes the paren. (`Callable[int(int)] g = (^(…))` is not
#     the cell to use: that spelling does not typecheck at all,
#     E_ClosureKindMismatch.)
#
# Wired to RUN: the point of the last two cells is that the ownership reading
# survives, and only a build+run proves it.

int apply_once(ConsumeCallable[int(int)] f, int x):
    return f(x)

void main():
    int n = 5
    print(apply_once((^(int x): x + n), 3))
    ConsumeCallable[int(int)] g = (^(int x): x + 1)
    print(apply_once(g, 1))
